## Orbit Salvage — complete, verified on the public game ✅

**Summary:** Compact playable browser game in a single `index.html` (no build step). Pilot a salvage drone in a circular orbital arena with WASD/arrow keys, collect drifting yellow scrap (+10 each), and dodge 3 red debris hazards on different orbit radii/speeds. HUD shows score, hull meter, and scrap/best (best persists via localStorage). Debris hits cost 34 hull with invulnerability frames + screen shake; 3 hits destroy the drone and show a "Drone Destroyed" overlay relaunchable via button, `R`, `Enter`, or `Space`. Inline favicon keeps the page free of console errors.

**Public game:** https://creature-courage-really-tony.trycloudflare.com — verified live: page loads (HTTP 200, correct 14,898-byte build), plays, and restarts.

**Final commit:** https://github.com/AgentsLoop/PlayGround/commit/4d6bfedc6c88997a72d4a20e360803520033fc84 (branch `opencode/34002160737`: `index.html` + final screenshots)

**Deployment status:** Code and screenshots committed and pushed on `opencode/34002160737`. No pull request created — left for the workflow.

**Test status:** Real-browser verified with headless Chromium directly against the public URL — all passing, zero console errors:
- Launch → `play` state, canvas renders
- Keyboard steering moves drone (~212px displacement)
- Exactly 3 rotating debris hazards present
- Scrap collection awards +10 and respawns
- 3 × 34 damage → hull 0, `dead` state, "Drone Destroyed" overlay visible
- `R` restart resets to score 0 / hull 100 with overlay hidden

**Known limitations:** None.

